Z||000000||Indiana_resto_guy||10-04-2000||11:52 PM||||I was planning a trip up to Dave's place this morning and was just about to walk out the door when he called.<BR>As things turned out the trip was postponed till next week.<BR>I had talked with him Monday to finalize my ETA, and he had complained of a neck injury obtained during the weekend while mowing the grass. The pain was still persistent this A.M.<BR>I changed my mind about running up his direction this week and talked him into going to the Emergency Room to be checked out instead.<BR>As this turns out, it was not a neck injury after all but some sort of infection in his nervous system. The condition is not serious but very annoying to him. At this time he has some problems focusing on the screen and reading messages as his eye(s) are constantly watering! (Can you imagine crying 24-7?) The Dr. also has him on some GOOD painkillers, which makes him higher than a kite with no tail, (heaven for some people!) so his attention span is also below normal!<BR>Anyway, he will be somewhat slower than normal in his response time, so if you send a message be patient, he'll get with you A.S.A.P. (condition prevailing)<BR>I will be going up there next week for sure and will also be glad to relay any important messages in the mean time or at that time.<BR>Any other concerns please ask!<P>||||reg||12
